+
+### Post-publication OCI conformance and materialization hardening
+
+The preceding pre-smoke statement is retained as chronology. The declared live
+OCI component smoke subsequently ran against exact published head
+`b7b008b52fcfb053dc8b6c25893c4dcaf475dc28`, tree
+`e436776d3a772544bf01cc718e5e4edc20194619`, in GitHub Actions run
+[36132076440](https://github.com/ktogias/gnostoa/actions/runs/36132076440), job
+`108061408916`. The one-shot workflow used `contents: read`, no Environment,
+secret or external input, and the already pinned image
+`ghcr.io/ktogias/gnostoa@sha256:f89bf32c0c4b86bac71fa008579b2385e6ae39bf4822f685479c4f2cc22bfca4`.
+Retained artifact `10862250915` matched provider archive SHA-256
+`87d908f59bbe446bfa22be22457142e80aecc45fed4c64d5ecec8036dc3feee4`
+before ZIP parsing; bounded `result.json` SHA-256 is
+`9dd838d5801fb67b20fe8e50df3656b31c0e85fc09d69acb96b1c9eb7b8594ca`.
+
+The fixed cases observed isolation and spoof cases completing with exit 0,
+nonzero exit 17, descendant timeout, bounded output overflow at 65,536 retained
+bytes, two successful successive immutable subjects with distinct commit/tree
+identities, and wrong-tree refusal before container start. Every executed case
+reported the subject unchanged and no authority effect. The retained result
+keeps `production_receipt_issued=false`, `producer_admitted=false`,
+`compliance_established=false` and `vf0_active=false`. This is actual Docker
+component conformance, not RED certification, producer admission, D0090
+activation or merge authority. Support-workflow cleanup commit
+`eace1d2c93235f02b4c4287a0c2e5265a6f10d40` restored its source tree; retained
+evidence expires 2026-10-02T11:56:11Z.
+
+Current-head CodeQL then supplied two pre-edit security findings on the Git
+materialization implementation: Python recomputed the Git SHA-1 blob object ID
+from blob bytes, and those same bytes were written from a Python value into the
+private materialization. The integrity requirement remains valid, but neither
+operation needs Python to hold repository blob content. The successor therefore
+streams `git cat-file blob` directly into an exclusively created destination,
+checks exact size/type, asks trusted Git to recompute the raw blob identity with
+`git hash-object --no-filters`, and retains only a SHA-256 file manifest in
+Python. A corruption regression replaces a loose object behind its expected
+object name and requires `SUBJECT_BLOB_MISMATCH` before backend execution. This
+hardening removes the weak-hash and clear-text-storage scanner patterns without
+weakening exact Git-object verification or changing the provider-neutral
+execution contract.
